ev-01045,obj-phy-212-download-119284452,parsed_download_text,download_binary_parsed,2053526,PHY-212,00298-phy-212-assignment-detail-m1-00asy-general-physics-with-calculus-ph-212-400-u2026,https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2053526/quizzes/3169001,M1-00asy: GENERAL PHYSICS WITH CALCULUS (PH_212_400_U2026),,,dl-phy-212-0044,,/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/parsed_files/captured-0031-phy-212-119284452.md,file=/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/downloaded_files/PHY-212_119284452_M1-00.pdf; parsed=/Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/parsed_files/captured-0031-phy-212-119284452.md; parsed_text=# PHY-212_119284452_M1-00.pdf - course_code: PHY-212 - course_id: 2053526 - canvas_file_id: 119284452 - repo_file_path: /Users/jake/Developer/SU26/canvas/indexer/output/downloaded_files/PHY-212_119284452_M1-00.pdf - download_ids: dl-phy-212-0044|dl-phy-212-0098|dl-phy-212-0099|dl-phy-212-0100 - download_manifest_ids: download-0044|download-0098|download-0099|download-0100 - source_page_titles: Jacob Peterson's Quiz History: M1-00asy|M1-00asy: GENERAL PHYSICS WITH CALCULUS (PH_212_400_U2026) ## Extracted Text # M1-00 Header: M1-00; Jacob Peterson; student ID visible on page. ## Problem 1 Set angular velocity to zero when it reverses direction: 0 = A - B t^2 t = sqrt(A / B) = sqrt(18 / 0.50) = sqrt(36) = 6.0 Answer: 6.0 ## Problem 2 The disk reverses at t = 6.0 s. Angular displacement: Delta theta = integral from 0 to 6 of (A - B t^2) dt Delta theta = A t - (B / 3) t^3 Delta theta = 18(6.0) - (0.50 / 3)(6.0)^3 Delta theta = 108 - 36 = 72 Answer: 72
